# 61-gs-shuffle-texreuse: two shuffle passes instead of four, and skip texture re-decodes whose source is unchanged.
#
# 1) Shuffle (gs_hw_backend.cpp, tryShuffle/flushShuffle): the source halfword used to be a uniform, so one state run
#    uploaded and drew up to four quad buckets (source half x destination half). It is now a per-vertex attribute; the
#    destination half still selects the colour mask (the two halves are written separately so the untouched half keeps
#    its pixels), so a run needs at most two uploads and two draws. The vertices also go through the patch 59 persistent
#    ring (glBindVertexBuffer with the shuffle stride) instead of glBufferData, when the ring is available
#    (GOW_GS_HW_RING=0 keeps the old buffer path).
#
# 2) Textures (textureFor / indexTextureFor): BeginTransfer invalidates every texture whose 256 B block span overlaps the
#    upload, and the next draw decoded the whole texture again even when the bytes it reads were not touched (or were
#    rewritten identically). The decode now records XXH64 of the GS memory span it reads [blockLo, blockHi); on the next
#    invalidation the same span is hashed again and, on a match, the live GL image is revalidated instead of decoded.
#    GOW_GS_TEXREUSE=0 turns the shortcut off.
#
# Measured (i3-4170 + HD 4400, Asia disc, fast boot attract/replay demo, 5 s windows, 0.5x internal, VU1 x64 fast):
#   baseline       guest 32.3-35.0 fps  gs_ms 1984-2180  texDecodes 1641-1751  texHits 5225-5588
#   61 (this)      guest 33.7-35.6 fps  gs_ms 2003-2194  texDecodes  843- 906  texReuse 842-891  texHits 6210-6668
#   shuffles are unchanged (5248-5600 per 5 s); shuffleDraws 1344-1448 per 5 s, at most two per state run.
# The frame rate is unchanged inside the noise of this scene: VU1 (4.52-4.57 s/5 s) and the frontend per-primitive cost
# (draws 2.3-3.0 M per 5 s) dominate it; patch 61 halves redundant decode work but does not move the wall.
#
# Not done here (still open, see docs/RENDER-PIPELINE-HANDOFF-2026-11-04.zh-CN.md section 9): per-primitive frontend
# submission (range draws), coarse per-frame flush reduction (the canonical state comparison was already measured as a
